Thanks for all the encouraging advice!  Since I posted, I haven't gone
any deeper into the dungeon, but I *have* re-scoured the levels I've
already visited, and with quite the results!  One of the first things
I did was to go back through the gnomish mines, looking for any good
boots or gauntlets I may have missed.  I found neither, but I *did*
find a bones pile from one of my old protection racket healers.  (more
on that later).  By the time I was finished with the mines, I had a
few more potions, the key I should have had from that shopkeeper, a
few more scrolls, a +5 elven mithril suit, and... (the big score) a +0
shield of reflection from a newly-spawned Aleax!

After all that, the next order of business was to fix my luck.  I
opted to empty my bag of tricks by the Dlvl4 altar.  I'm fairly
certain, by the way, that Pat Rankin is right.  By all rights I should
have been wasting my time, as the monsters who would have spawned at
that level wouldn't have done anything to quell Tyr's anger.
However... the 2nd-to-last monster to pop out of that bag was a gray
unicorn.  "Tyr seems mollified."

Having restored my ability to pray, I set to the task of collecting
water.  First the unicorn horn, then a zap of my cancellation wand,
and finally, a trip to dry out the oracle's fountains.  I saved a
handful of object detection and booze potions in case I needed them
later, and ended up with 25 uncursed water.  One prayer later, and I
was in business!

Armed with plenty of holy water, I immediately blessed my luckstone,
bag of holding, and a potion of see invisible for the intrinsic.  I
proceeded to write three additional identify scrolls for a total of
six, then dip the stack.  I carefully filled my inventory with nothing
but items that I'd like identified, including charged items, with the
lowest priority going to gems.  With six identify scrolls, I didn't
get so lucky as to roll a full ID, but I definitely identified
everything important.  Among my scrolls was remove curse, so I blessed
that and uncursed everything except the create monster and teleport
scrolls.

Here are the most significant finds:

 an uncursed ring of slow digestion (from the bones file, originally
cursed)
 an uncursed ring of shock resistance (wore it for about half an hour,
then finally got the intrinsic from a gelatinous cube and swapped it
for =oSD)
 an uncursed ring of polymorph
 an uncursed ring of sustain ability

 a wand of secret door detection (0:14)  (and two with unknown
charges; those 150 zorkmid wands were all the same)
 a wand of fire (0:3)  (from a soldier while going back down and up
the levels)

 a magic marker (0:77)
 a magic marker (0:49)

 an uncursed +0 pair of elven boots (the jungle boots)

Not as useful included:

 an uncursed amulet of strangulation (oh, well)
 an uncursed ring of teleportation
 an uncursed ring of cold resistance
 an uncursed -1 ring of increase accuracy

 an uncursed scroll of punishment

 other new, useful additions include:

 an uncursed pair of lenses
 an uncursed tinning kit
 an uncursed harp
 an uncursed key
 an uncursed stethoscope


So!  Equipped with a source of reflection, slow digestion, 3 charges
of permanent elbereth, a couple more intrinsics, 2 magic markers, some
paper, and lots of holy water, I feel confident to venture onto my
quest!  The biggest thing I'm itching for now is a source of MR, but I
think I'll be OK long enough to get my hands on something.  BTW... it
turns out my quest portal level has another opulent throne.  I'll work
on my luck a bit more (I've already earned 4 or 5 clovers through
sacrificing), then give it a careful shot.

Thanks again for all the help!

